WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.838 --> 00:00:18.501
By the next afternoon, Perda knew she'd been right to insist on staying in Terrica.

2
00:00:18.521 --> 00:00:22.483
"This is wild," she whispered to Zann and Mellis.

3
00:00:23.063 --> 00:00:25.405
The three of them were at the edge of the village green.

4
00:00:26.345 --> 00:00:30.748
Vilkor was in the center of the green, standing on a golden dais he'd created.

5
00:00:31.476 --> 00:00:33.017
Zira was seated behind him.

6
00:00:33.637 --> 00:00:37.500
Dozens of villagers were gathered around the dais, chanting Vilkor's name.

7
00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:39.521
"Next, please!"

8
00:00:39.941 --> 00:00:40.721
Vilkor shouted.

9
00:00:41.402 --> 00:00:43.003
He pointed at a woman in the crowd.

10
00:00:43.023 --> 00:00:44.564
"You there.

11
00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:48.386
Come forward and tell me what you wish me to provide for you."

12
00:00:49.546 --> 00:00:50.867
The woman shuffled forward.

13
00:00:50.887 --> 00:00:53.469
"Thank you, Vilkor," she said.

14
00:00:53.489 --> 00:00:56.370
"My cloak is old and worn."

15
00:00:57.071 --> 00:00:59.292
She fingered the tattered garment she was wearing.

16
00:01:00.032 --> 00:01:01.693
"May I please have a new one?"

17
00:01:01.713 --> 00:01:05.114
"Yes, I will do this for you."

18
00:01:05.914 --> 00:01:12.837
Vilkor closed his eyes, waved his arms dramatically and chanted a few nonsense words, and then clapped his

19
00:01:12.877 --> 00:01:15.358
hands. A beautiful cloak appeared.

20
00:01:15.979 --> 00:01:16.959
The crowd gasped.

21
00:01:17.659 --> 00:01:23.562
The woman dropped to her knees as Vilkor stepped forward to drape the cloak around her thin shoulders.

22
00:01:23.582 --> 00:01:25.823
"Thank you, Vilkor!"

23
00:01:26.143 --> 00:01:26.843
the woman cried.

24
00:01:26.863 --> 00:01:28.824
"Thank you so much!"

25
00:01:29.656 --> 00:01:33.078
"This is ridiculous," Perda muttered, feeling annoyed.

26
00:01:33.098 --> 00:01:37.441
"He's trying to fool everyone with all that muttering and arm waving.

27
00:01:38.122 --> 00:01:40.223
It's the clap that creates friction."

28
00:01:40.243 --> 00:01:43.345
"I know that, and you know that," Zann said.

29
00:01:43.365 --> 00:01:46.868
"But we can't tell anyone or Zira might punish Mellis."

30
00:01:47.728 --> 00:01:49.309
Perda glanced toward Zira.

31
00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:54.913
The woman had stayed close to Vilkor all day, but she was letting him get all the attention.

32
00:01:54.933 --> 00:01:57.315
"Hmm," Perda thought.

33
00:01:57.335 --> 00:01:58.836
"I wonder why."

34
00:01:59.944 --> 00:02:01.324
Another villager stepped forward.

35
00:02:01.344 --> 00:02:04.745
"That's my friend Anso's father," Mellis said.

36
00:02:04.765 --> 00:02:07.886
"My family has run out of bread," the man said.

37
00:02:07.906 --> 00:02:10.187
"We have no grain to make more.

38
00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:12.287
Please help me."

39
00:02:12.307 --> 00:02:15.248
"Oh no," Mellis said.

40
00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:17.189
"Of course, of course."

41
00:02:18.489 --> 00:02:23.831
Vilkor went through his routine again, ending with a clap and the appearance of a small loaf of

42
00:02:23.891 --> 00:02:27.912
bread. "Thank you," the man said as he accepted it.

43
00:02:29.004 --> 00:02:32.707
"But you see, I have a growing son, and my wife is ill.

44
00:02:33.368 --> 00:02:36.130
Could I have more bread so we all might have enough to eat?"

45
00:02:37.051 --> 00:02:38.011
Vilkor frowned.

46
00:02:38.031 --> 00:02:44.076
"How do I know you will share it with your family, rather than bartering it away to your

47
00:02:44.237 --> 00:02:45.077
own benefit?

48
00:02:46.078 --> 00:02:51.543
If your wife and son wish to have more to eat, they can come and beg me for

49
00:02:51.663 --> 00:02:52.844
bread themselves."

50
00:02:52.864 --> 00:02:57.908
"But my wife is ill, as I said," the man protested.

51
00:02:58.516 --> 00:03:02.039
"My son is staying with her in case her condition grows worse."

52
00:03:03.139 --> 00:03:05.341
"Begone!" Vilkor insisted.

53
00:03:05.361 --> 00:03:11.025
"Do not question my decisions, or next time you might receive nothing at all!"

54
00:03:11.945 --> 00:03:12.846
Mellis gasped.

55
00:03:14.467 --> 00:03:15.308
Zann winced.

56
00:03:15.888 --> 00:03:18.870
"Wow! All this power is really going to Vilkor's head."

57
00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:22.813
"I have to help Anso and his family," Mellis said.

58
00:03:23.473 --> 00:03:27.496
Perda nodded as she watched Anso's father make his way through the crowd.

59
00:03:28.064 --> 00:03:29.285
The man looked sad.

60
00:03:29.305 --> 00:03:31.346
"Come with me," Perda said.

61
00:03:32.307 --> 00:03:35.909
She hurried to intercept the man as he reached the edge of the green.

62
00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:38.031
Zann and Mellis followed.

63
00:03:38.611 --> 00:03:42.354
The man saw them coming and smiled, but his eyes remained worried.

64
00:03:42.374 --> 00:03:44.975
"Hello, Mellis," he said.

65
00:03:44.995 --> 00:03:47.457
"I hope you'll come to visit Anso soon.

66
00:03:48.338 --> 00:03:51.179
He's been busy helping his mother, but I know he'd love to see you."

67
00:03:51.199 --> 00:03:55.542
"We saw what just happened," Perda said before Mellis could respond.

68
00:03:55.562 --> 00:03:57.704
"Come with us and we'll help you."

69
00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:00.140
The man looked surprised.

70
00:04:00.441 --> 00:04:02.581
But he followed Perda to a deserted alley.

71
00:04:04.882 --> 00:04:10.003
She created several loaves of bread, along with cheese and fruit and a bag to carry it in.

72
00:04:10.023 --> 00:04:11.224
"Thank you!"

73
00:04:11.964 --> 00:04:13.224
The man looked overwhelmed.

74
00:04:13.244 --> 00:04:16.065
"But how are you doing that?

75
00:04:16.705 --> 00:04:19.166
I thought only Vilkor had gained the power of magic."

76
00:04:19.186 --> 00:04:22.447
"That's what he wants you to think," Zann said.

77
00:04:23.187 --> 00:04:23.927
Perda nodded.

78
00:04:23.947 --> 00:04:25.788
"Anyone can do magic.

79
00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:29.522
All you have to do is create friction, and then—" "Perda!

80
00:04:29.922 --> 00:04:32.163
No!" Mellis looked frightened.

81
00:04:32.183 --> 00:04:34.365
"What if Zira finds out?"

82
00:04:34.785 --> 00:04:35.145
"Heads up!"

83
00:04:35.685 --> 00:04:36.326
Zann hissed.

84
00:04:37.006 --> 00:04:38.607
"Isn't that Zira's friend, what's his name?"

85
00:04:38.627 --> 00:04:42.229
"Krub," Perda said, recognizing the man.

86
00:04:42.870 --> 00:04:45.511
He walked past the end of the alley without noticing them.

87
00:04:45.531 --> 00:04:48.333
"Whew," Mellis said.

88
00:04:48.353 --> 00:04:50.374
"That was a close call.

89
00:04:51.194 --> 00:04:53.516
Krub always does everything Zira says.

90
00:04:54.188 --> 00:04:56.969
He probably would have told her about seeing us here."

91
00:04:57.749 --> 00:04:59.609
Anso's father looked nervous too.

92
00:04:59.629 --> 00:05:04.351
"Thank you, young friends," he said, clutching the bag of food to his chest.

93
00:05:04.371 --> 00:05:06.791
"I'd better go home and check on my wife."

94
00:05:07.892 --> 00:05:08.752
He scurried away.

95
00:05:09.552 --> 00:05:13.313
Perda was disappointed that she hadn't had the chance to teach him basic magic.

96
00:05:13.853 --> 00:05:16.134
But she could tell that Mellis was relieved.

97
00:05:17.054 --> 00:05:19.755
"I know you're scared," she told the Terrican girl.

98
00:05:19.775 --> 00:05:23.736
"But surely by now you see that we have to stop this.

99
00:05:24.488 --> 00:05:27.329
What your uncle and Zira are doing is wrong."

100
00:05:27.349 --> 00:05:28.949
"I know."

101
00:05:29.710 --> 00:05:30.950
Mellis looked miserable.

102
00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:35.391
"I hate seeing my uncle force everyone to grovel before him.

103
00:05:36.011 --> 00:05:37.172
But what can we do?"

104
00:05:37.192 --> 00:05:40.092
"We can stand up to them," Zann said.

105
00:05:40.113 --> 00:05:41.293
"We have to."

106
00:05:42.233 --> 00:05:44.914
Perda smiled at him, glad that he was backing her up.

107
00:05:45.594 --> 00:05:50.115
She'd thought he might not, since he was so eager to return to Magica the day before.

108
00:05:50.796 --> 00:05:52.016
She wanted to go home too.

109
00:05:52.820 --> 00:05:57.802
She missed her family and friends, and she hated that they were surely worried sick about her and

110
00:05:57.842 --> 00:06:01.243
Zann. But they would understand when they heard the whole story.

111
00:06:01.263 --> 00:06:02.724
"What do you say?"

112
00:06:03.064 --> 00:06:04.125
Perda asked Mellis.

113
00:06:04.145 --> 00:06:06.325
"Will you help us put a stop to this?"

114
00:06:07.366 --> 00:06:08.326
Mellis hesitated.

115
00:06:08.346 --> 00:06:09.547
"I'll try.

116
00:06:09.567 --> 00:06:14.529
But I still don't believe my uncle will be able to keep up this charade for long.

117
00:06:15.309 --> 00:06:18.110
In the meantime, will you teach me more magic?

118
00:06:18.650 --> 00:06:22.492
Then I can start teaching Anso and some of the other kids in secret.

119
00:06:23.136 --> 00:06:26.118
That way we'll be ready once the truth finally comes out."

120
00:06:26.959 --> 00:06:29.600
It wasn't quite the plan Perda would have chosen.

121
00:06:30.121 --> 00:06:35.244
But she had to admit it sounded a lot safer for Mellis, at least while Vilkor and Zira

122
00:06:35.304 --> 00:06:35.925
were in charge.
